  "question": {
    "text": "To establish an instantaneous current of $2 \\mathrm{~A}$ through a $1 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ capacitor ; the potential difference across the capacitor plates should be changed at the rate of:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\times 10^4 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4 \\times 10^4 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As, C $=\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{\\mathrm{V}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{It}}{\\mathrm{V}}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{t}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{2}{1 \\times 10^{-6}} \\\\\n& =2 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
